From: Chen Minqiang <ptpt52@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt7996: report the receive WED for RX path queries

MT7996 uses the main WED for RRO receive queues even when a station's
transmit path uses the second PCIe interface. Return the actual receive
WED for explicit RX queries so NATflow installs uplink flows in the PPE
that receives the traffic and records the correct WED ownership.

Keep transmit queries and kernels without the RX query extension on the
existing path. Require a receive-capable main WED before reporting RX.

Signed-off-by: Chen Minqiang <ptpt52@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt7996/main.c
+++ b/mt7996/main.c
@@ -3317,6 +3317,14 @@
 	if (!mtk_wed_device_active(wed) &&
 	    !mt76_npu_device_active(&dev->mt76))
 		return -ENODEV;
+#ifdef NET_DEVICE_PATH_MTK_WDMA_RX
+	if (ctx->mtk_wdma_rx) {
+		/* All RRO receive queues use the main WED, including band 2. */
+		wed = &dev->mt76.mmio.wed;
+		if (!mtk_wed_device_active(wed) || !mtk_wed_get_rx_capa(wed))
+			return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+	}
+#endif
 	/* The new natflow AP path needs peer/key lifetime validation. Keep
 	 * the existing forward-path behavior for other interface modes.
 	 */
